\section{push-pull dyanmics analogy in psychology}
Anxious + anvoidant relationships.
Anxious partner pulls in avoidants 
but they get too close and avoidant partner pushes awy anxious partner.

Litter pulls in Avena and then medusahead gets pushed out.
The litter is kindof like the "crazy-ness" that the anxious partner creates
or like the situation theyre using to pull in the avoidant partner.
Medusahead is anxious needs closeness so it makes litter to pull
in its avoidant partner, Avena. But then the litter than the
anxious partner made itself causes the anxious partner to be pushed out.
(And Avena competion?). Some sort of lag. 

Push pull dynamics describe many things in the natural world. 
Human migration, supply chain, cellular and biochemical processes..
Range shifts

Previous studies model and experimentally show oscillating
bistatbility of cell states depending on external
signal (baceteria) or resource (yeast, Krishna 2018)
They call it "asynchronous, heterogenous cultures of cells"
-asynchronus through time; heterogenous through space




